[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### A9 — input shapes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Pattern: empty, 1 unit, many units, 40 000 units, embedded NUL, explicit length
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m vs `PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED`, ASCII vs multi-byte UTF-8 vs invalid UTF-8,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 250/251 nesting depth, 10 001 named groups, 6 000-range class.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Subject: empty (`NULL`+0 and pointer+0), 1, 2, 255, 256, 1 000, 5 000 units;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m explicit length vs `PCRE2_ZERO_TERMINATED`; embedded NUL; every newline sequence
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`\n`, `\r`, `\r\n`, `\x85`, U+2028/9); valid and invalid UTF-8; every start
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m offset from 0 to `len`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Ovector: `create(0)`, `create(1)`, `create(8)`, `create_from_pattern`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `create(65535)`, `create(65536)`, `create(UINT32_MAX)`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    115[0m:[38;5;10m[49m Output buffers (substitute / substring / convert): capacities 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 8,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    116[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 16, 48, 256.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    117[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    118[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## How each row is checked
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    119[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    120[0m:[38;5;10m[49m For every row, both `.so`s are driven through their exported symbols with **many
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    121[0m:[38;5;10m[49m randomized inputs** (fixed seeds, see the `Rng::new(...)` calls) and the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    122[0m:[38;5;10m[49m following are compared:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    123[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1. `pcre2_compile`: NULL-ness, `*errorcode`, `*erroroffset`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 2. The **entire compiled byte code, byte for byte** — obtained with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `pcre2_serialize_encode`, which dumps the whole `pcre2_real_code` block plus
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    the character tables. This is what makes the untestable internal helpers
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    (`_pcre2_study`, `_pcre2_auto_possessify`, the class compilers, the name-table
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    builder) verifiable: any difference in what they produce changes these bytes.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 3. Every `pcre2_pattern_info` item, including `FIRSTBITMAP` (32 bytes) and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    131[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `NAMETABLE` (`namecount * nameentrysize` bytes).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    132[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 4. `pcre2_code_copy` and `pcre2_code_copy_with_tables` byte code.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    133[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 5. `pcre2_match`, `pcre2_dfa_match` (workspace 20 / 64 / 1000, with and without
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    134[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `DFA_SHORTEST`, plus `DFA_RESTART` after a partial match) and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    135[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `pcre2_jit_match`: return code, the defined part of the ovector,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    136[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `pcre2_get_startchar`, `pcre2_get_mark`, `pcre2_get_match_data_size`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    137[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `pcre2_next_match`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    138[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 6. All substring accessors for groups 0..5 (`length_bynumber`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    139[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `copy_bynumber` at several capacities, `get_bynumber`, `list_get`).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    140[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 7. Callout blocks: every field of `pcre2_callout_block` and
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    141[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    `pcre2_callout_enumerate_block`, in order, for accepting / skipping /
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    142[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    aborting callbacks.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    143[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 8. The allocation *sequence*: a counting allocator records every requested size,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    144[0m:[38;5;10m[49m    and the two sequences must be identical.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    145[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    146[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Feature combinations
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    147[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    148[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `translation/Cargo.toml` declares **no `[features]` table**, so the crate has
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    149[0m:[38;5;10m[49m exactly one feature combination: `--no-default-features` and the default build
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    150[0m:[38;5;10m[49m are the same thing. `tools/check_features.sh` enumerates the features from
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    151[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `Cargo.toml` and runs `cargo check` / `cargo test` for each combination; it
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    152[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reports the single (empty) combination.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    153[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
